sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Sign in or reopen during an active login
    accDescr: WinUI prechecks the Master Password and vault integrity before asking for an OTP. Final unlock repeats cryptographic checks inside the serialized runner. New login requires a current OTP and gets a fixed five-hour deadline; reopening an active login uses only the Master Password and preserves the deadline. Legacy recovery-key enrollment blocks ordinary workspace access until confirmed.
    participant U as User
    participant V as WinUI
    participant F as AppFlowCoordinator
    participant C as Core vault
    U->>V: Enter Master Password
    V->>F: ValidateMasterPasswordAsync
    F->>C: Serialized password and payload precheck
    C-->>F: Precheck result, no login created
    F-->>V: Valid or invalid
    break Invalid password or unreadable vault
        V-->>U: Keep sign-in screen, show error
    end
    alt No active five-hour login
        V->>U: Ask for current Authenticator code
        U-->>V: Enter current six-digit code
    else Login remains active
        V->>V: Skip OTP prompt
        Note over V,C: Reopening never extends the existing login
    end
    break User cancels the prompt
        V-->>U: Keep vault locked
    end
    V->>F: UnlockAsync(password, code)
    F->>C: Recheck password, unwrap DEK and decrypt
    F->>C: Verify OTP or existing login authorization
    alt Invalid, expired or lifecycle changed
        C->>C: Lock vault, clear decrypted state
        F-->>V: Failed or cancelled
    else Authorized
        C->>C: New login only: now + five hours
        C->>C: Vault deadline capped by login expiry
        F-->>V: Unlock or require Recovery Key enrollment
        V-->>U: Workspace after enrollment is complete
    end
